000100 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
000200 PROGRAM-ID. FDRECS.
000300* An FD may describe its record more than one way. The 01s are not
000400* separate areas: each describes the same buffer, implicitly
000500* redefining the first, and the file's record length is the
000600* longest of them. WRITE may name any of them, and FROM fills the
000700* one that was named.
000800 ENVIRONMENT DIVISION.
000900 INPUT-OUTPUT SECTION.
001000 FILE-CONTROL.
001100     SELECT OUT-FILE ASSIGN TO UT-S-OUTFILE.
001200 DATA DIVISION.
001300 FILE SECTION.
001400 FD  OUT-FILE
001500     LABEL RECORDS ARE OMITTED.
001600 01  HEADER-REC.
001700     02  H-TAG    PIC X(4).
001800     02  H-TEXT   PIC X(26).
001900 01  DETAIL-REC.
002000     02  D-TAG    PIC X(4).
002100     02  D-NUM    PIC 9(6).
002200     02  D-NAME   PIC X(20).
002300 01  WHOLE-REC    PIC X(30).
002400 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
002500 01  BUILT        PIC X(30)
002600     VALUE 'FROMBUILT IN WORKING-STORAGE  '.
002700 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
002800     OPEN OUTPUT OUT-FILE.
002900     MOVE 'HDR ' TO H-TAG.
003000     MOVE 'A HEADER LINE             ' TO H-TEXT.
003100     WRITE HEADER-REC.
003200     MOVE 'DTL ' TO D-TAG.
003300     MOVE 42 TO D-NUM.
003400     MOVE 'FORTY-TWO           ' TO D-NAME.
003500     WRITE DETAIL-REC.
003600     MOVE 'WHOLEREC WRITTEN AS ONE FIELD ' TO WHOLE-REC.
003700     WRITE WHOLE-REC.
003800     WRITE DETAIL-REC FROM BUILT.
003900* The buffer is shared, so the last WRITE left BUILT's bytes in
004000* every one of the three descriptions.
004100     WRITE WHOLE-REC.
004200     CLOSE OUT-FILE.
004300     STOP RUN.
